title: Multiple Failed Logon Attempts (Possible Brute Force)
id: 8c1e0f2a-1b3d-4e2a-9f6c-1a2b3c4d5e6f
status: stable
description: >
  Detects 5 or more failed logon attempts (Event ID 4625) for the same
  target account within a 5 minute window, which may indicate a
  brute-force or password-guessing attempt.
author: Parin Bhikha
date: 2026/08/01
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1110/
tags:
  - attack.credential_access
  - attack.t1110
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: security
detection:
  selection:
    EventID: 4625
  timeframe: 5m
  condition: selection | count(TargetUserName) by TargetUserName >= 5
falsepositives:
  - Users who have forgotten their password
  - Misconfigured service accounts retrying with stale credentials
level: medium







title: Scheduled Task Created (Possible Persistence)
id: 5d6e7f8a-9b0c-4d1e-8f2a-3b4c5d6e7f8a
status: stable
description: >
  Detects creation of a new scheduled task (Event ID 4698), particularly
  where the action references a temp directory or user-writable path —
  a common persistence technique.
author: Parin Bhikha
date: 2026/08/01
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/005/
tags:
  - attack.persistence
  - attack.t1053.005
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: security
detection:
  selection:
    EventID: 4698
  suspicious_path:
    TaskContent|contains:
      - '\AppData\Local\Temp\'
      - '\Users\Public\'
      - '\ProgramData\'
  condition: selection and suspicious_path
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate software installers that register scheduled tasks
    (e.g., update checkers) — verify the binary and publisher
level: medium







title: Suspicious PowerShell Execution via Encoded Command
id: 2f4a6b8c-3d5e-4f7a-8b9c-0d1e2f3a4b5c
status: stable
description: >
  Detects PowerShell being launched with the -EncodedCommand (or -enc)
  flag, a common technique used to obfuscate malicious commands and
  evade simple string-based detection.
author: Parin Bhikha
date: 2026/08/01
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/001/
tags:
  - attack.execution
  - attack.t1059.001
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: windows
detection:
  selection:
    Image|endswith: '\powershell.exe'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '-enc '
      - '-EncodedCommand'
      - '-e '
  condition: selection
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate administrative scripts that use encoded commands for
    non-malicious reasons (verify parent process and decoded content)
level: high
